843	Diabenol-PE	Active	2	Natural Origin	<p><strong style="color: rgb(47, 49, 55); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Diabetes (capsule): Price: </strong><strong>149 PEN</strong></p><p></p><p><a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/13Zl15dEav-iK2qmoFgi8p3NPRupQv2Jt" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(31, 115, 173); background-color: transparent;">CREATIVES l PRODUCT INFO</a></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">INGREDIENTS</span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">- YACON</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Yacon is generally considered good for diabetes management, primarily due to its high concentration of fructooligosaccharides (FOS), a type of prebiotic fiber that does not spike blood sugar and can improve insulin sensitivity. Studies suggest yacon consumption, particularly for over 8 weeks, can help reduce fasting blood sugar and LDL cholesterol, especially in individuals over 40. </span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">- PASUCHACA</strong></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Is a Peruvian Andean herb traditionally used to manage diabetes, primarily for its reported hypoglycemic properties that help lower blood sugar levels and stimulate pancreatic activity. Studies it assists with Type 2 diabetes by inhibiting \\(\\alpha \\)-glucosidase and reducing blood sugar.</span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">- CUTI CUTI</strong></p><p></p><p><em style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Blechnum asplenioides</em><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">, a fern used in traditional Peruvian medicine, shows potential as a natural supplement to manage diabetes by lowering blood glucose and cholesterol levels. Studies indicate it contains compounds like flavonoids and phenolics, which may assist in regulating hyperglycemic levels.</span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">- ALCACHOFA</strong></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Is considered an excellent food for managing diabetes and for people with prediabetes due to their high fiber content and ability to help regulate blood sugar levels. They are low in calories and contain compounds that can improve insulin sensitivity and support heart health</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Rich in Inulin: Artichokes are a significant source of inulin, a type of prebiotic fiber that acts as a fructan, which the body metabolizes without requiring insulin, making it ideal for diabetics.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Regulates Blood Sugar: The high fiber content (soluble and insoluble) slows the absorption of sugar into the bloodstream, preventing sharp spikes or drops in glucose levels.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Improves Insulin Sensitivity: Studies have shown that consuming artichoke can improve the function of pancreatic cells and enhance the effect of insulin.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">  </span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Reduces Postprandial Glucose: Consuming artichoke during a meal has been shown to reduce blood sugar and insulin levels 30 minutes after eating.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Contains Antioxidants: They are rich in antioxidants, including cynarin and chlorogenic acid, which help reduce inflammation and improve heart health, which is vital for people with diabetes. </span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">- CÚRCUMA</strong></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Specifically its active compound </span><strong style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">curcumin</strong><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">, shows significant promise in helping to manage diabetes, prediabetes, and associated complications. Studies suggest it improves insulin sensitivity, lowers blood sugar levels, and reduces inflammation, with studies finding that 80 mg/day for 12 weeks lowered HbA1c in older adults.</span></p><p></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">PRESENTATION: 30 CAPSULES PER BOTTLE</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">TARGET: 30+ y.o – men and women</span></p><p></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">USE: 1 CAPSULE 2 TIMES A DAT WITH WATER. PREFERABLY ONE IN THE MORNING AND ONE AT NIGHT.</span></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">RESTRICTIONS: Keep away from kids. Keep in a cool, dry place. </span></p><p></p><p><strong style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">MADE IN EUROPE</strong></p><p></p>		https://admin.affscale.com/manager/offers/new/wizard/general	https://admin.affscale.com/manager/offers/new/wizard/general	Diabetes, Peru	Diabetes, Peru		USD		2026-07-13 04:02:59	2026-05-08 03:51:12	861	Approved Lead	CPA	22.0000	18.0000	Active			2026-07-27 04:28:38.800051+00
